<title>HONG KONG: Sino Land details HK site development.</title>
<headline>Sino Land details HK site development.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sino Land Co Ltd chairman Robert Ng said on Tuesday a site bought by the company and his family at a government land auction would be developed for residential and commercial purposes.</p>
<p>He told reporters the Chai Wan site would be developed into a complex with 300,000 square feet of shopping area and two million square feet of residential area.</p>
<p>A consortium equally owned by Sino Land and the Ng family bought the site for HK$11.82 billion, a record price fetched at government land auctions.</p>
<p>Ng said total investment for the development would be about HK$20 billion.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6590</p>
